    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a favorable slate today, anchored by **Nasim Nunez**, who earns our highest grade at 64.14. Despite being projected in the bottom third of the order, **Nasim Nunez** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Ryan Feltner; his elite sprint speed and the favorable 5.10 xERA of the opposing starter make him an essential play for stolen base upside. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** represents a strong play at 59.34. Leading off against Kumar Rocker allows **Sam Antonacci** to capitalize on a +10% order bonus and a +7% platoon edge, making him a high-efficiency contributor for Runs and AVG despite Rocker\u2019s respectable 4.36 xERA.\n\nWhile **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) sit in the marginal-to-strong transition zone, they provide necessary stability. **Miguel Vargas** is buoyed by a +6% order bonus hitting third, helping offset a neutral park factor. Conversely, **Tommy White** (55.05) remains a solid consideration due to a +10% park factor that compensates for a neutral matchup against Zebby Matthews. The most difficult bench decision was strictly dictated by the calendar; our studs **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, forcing us to rely on this depth tier to maximize our daily game caps. \n\nInvestors should monitor the lineup cards closely, as **Liam Hicks** (49.04) carries significant risk; while he is currently slotted for a +5% wind-aided boost, his score is suppressed by a negative platoon differential against the southpaw Framber Valdez. Should **Liam Hicks** drop in the order or be rested, we may pivot to our reserve depth to ensure we don't squander a starting slot on a poor efficiency outcome. With no elite aces on the opposing mound today, the path is clear for our speed-oriented roster to gain ground in the SB category.",
